  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_inputs",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "Sprite UV and the sprite texture."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_height",
        "position": {
          "x": 768,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1460
        },
        "text": "`luma` (Rec. 709) of the sprite colour is the height; `saturate((luma − ½) × contrast + ½)` widens the range so mortar lines, rivets and shading become real grooves."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_normal",
        "position": {
          "x": 2432,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 90,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "The **Height To Normal** node (*derivative* quality) turns `dHeight/dx, dHeight/dy` into a tangent-space normal `normalize(−slope·strength, 1)`. *Packed* = `normal × ½ + ½` for the debug view. Output goes to the profile's **Normal (Tangent Space)** slot, which the 2D Lights shade."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_color",
        "position": {
          "x": 2432,
          "y": 590
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 848
        },
        "text": "Sprite colour × tint; with *Show Normals* the packed normal replaces it (blue = facing the viewer)."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 3484,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Base colour, alpha and the generated tangent-space normal."
      }
    ],
